        "step_number": 1,
        "description": "Identify the coordinates of the points.",
        "expression": null
      },
      {
        "step_number": 2,
        "description": "Substitute the coordinates into the distance formula.",
        "expression": "d = \\sqrt{(4 - 2)^2 + (3 - 3)^2 + (1 - 5)^2}"
      },
      {
        "step_number": 3,
        "description": "Calculate the distance.",
        "expression": "d = \\sqrt{2^2 + 0^2 + (-4)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 0 + 16} = \\sqrt{20} = 2\\sqrt{5}"
      }
    ],
    "final_answer": "Therefore, the distance between the points (2, 3, 5) and (4, 3, 1) is 2\\sqrt{5}.",
